# SwiftUI Architecture Patterns

## View Structure

- Use `@StateObject` for ViewModels that manage complex state
- Use `@Published` properties for reactive UI updates
- Separate data models from view logic using dedicated service classes
- Prefer `@Binding` for child-to-parent communication over complex callback chains

## Data Flow

- ViewModels should handle business logic and data transformation
- Services should handle external integrations (EventKit, geocoding, etc.)
- Use `SessionFormModel` for form data handling to separate concerns
- Always validate data before applying to entities

## Form Handling

- Use `SessionFormModel` for session form data to separate validation from persistence
- Implement proper validation before any data application
- Use `SessionModificationService` for consistent entity creation/modification
- Avoid creating temporary entities for operations like geocoding

## Entity Management

- Use `SessionFactory` for consistent session creation across the app
- Always validate before saving to SwiftData
- Handle recurring sessions with proper dialog options (this only, this and future, all)
- Use proper error handling with specific error types

## UI Components

- Use glass morphism styling with `Color.black.opacity(0.3)` base and `Color.white.opacity(0.05)` hover
- Implement consistent hover effects with `.easeInOut(duration: 0.2)` animations
- Use `CustomHSplitView` instead of `NavigationSplitView` for split views
- Apply consistent border styling with accent colors

## Address Handling

- Use `AddressSearchField` component for address input
- Avoid creating temporary `AddressEntity` instances for geocoding
- Use direct `CLGeocoder` calls for address geocoding without persistence
- Only create `AddressEntity` instances during actual session save operations
